{"title":"Urban Data Analyst Roadmap","role":"Urban Data Analyst","summary":"An Urban Data Analyst combines geospatial technology, urban planning concepts, statistics, and data analytics to understand how cities function and support evidence-based decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Geoinformatics / Geomatics Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Urban Data Analyst combines geospatial technology, urban planning concepts, statistics, and data analytics to understand how cities function and support evidence-based decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"The role can involve analyzing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Population distribution"},{"text":"Land use and land cover"},{"text":"Urban growth"},{"text":"Transportation"},{"text":"Traffic patterns"},{"text":"Public infrastructure"},{"text":"Housing"},{"text":"Utilities"},{"text":"Environmental conditions"},{"text":"Real-estate patterns"},{"text":"Public services"},{"text":"Disaster risk"},{"text":"Mobility and accessibility"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A Geoinformatics/Geomatics graduate has a particularly strong foundation because urban data is often spatial data—where where something happens is as important as what happens."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build GIS, remote sensing, statistics, SQL, Python and urban-data skills; enter as GIS Analyst, Urban Data Analyst, Spatial Data Analyst or Geospatial Analyst."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Urban Data Analyst, Geospatial Data Scientist, Urban Analytics Specialist or Mobility Analyst."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Move into Urban Analytics Lead, Smart City Data Lead, Geospatial Solutions Manager or Urban Intelligence Consultant."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{